DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerFilm\n\n5:30 p.m. check in\n6:
 00 p.m. program\n\nAlso know: The speakers and audience will be videotaped
  for use on YouTube\, and audience questions may be included in the radio 
 and podcast versions of the show.\n\nLocation\n\n110 The Embarcadero\, San
  Francisco CA 94105\n\nDescription\n\nJoin Climate One\, in partnership wi
 th The Redford Center\, for a screening of the short film In Earth We Trus
 t\, followed by a conversation with the filmmaker\, the film’s central f
 igure\, and other faith leaders.\nFifteen years ago\, Reverend Richard Ciz
 ik had the attention of 30 million evangelical Christians and was generati
 ng momentum for a faith-based moral obligation to care for the planet. Thi
 s idea of “Creation Care” was controversial\, but Rev. Cizik became a 
 media darling – the face of the more reasonable modern-day evangelical 
 – until his outspoken ideals led others to force his resignation. This i
 s the story of how a man\, set on changing the world\, went from vice pres
 ident of one of the biggest religious organizations in America\, and one o
 f TIME Magazine’s top 100 influential people\, to becoming a part-time L
 yft driver\; the story of how he continues to influence hearts and minds w
 hen it comes to the environment\; and ultimately\, a story about finding c
 ommon ground in a polarized world.\nFollowing the film screening\, Climate
  One Executive Director Jenny Park will be joined by the film’s director
  Sophie Morgan\, Reverend Richard Cizik\, Rabbi Josh Weisman\, and Regina 
 Banks\, d...\n\n$27.50\n\nTickets: https://www.climateone.org/events/rev-r
 ichard-ciziks-route-altar-k-street-lyft-driver?utm_source=sf-weekly&amp\;u
 tm_medium=event-site\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/climate-film-screen
 ing-earth-trust-faith-leader-talk-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
