DESCRIPTION:Authors of two recent memoirs and one novel invite us to ride 
 along on a narrative journey through California.\n\nFREE\, $10–15 sugges
 ted donation\n\nCo-presented with LITQUAKE\n\nTaking the driver’s seat o
 n tonight’s narrative journey through California is Grant Faulkner\, who
 se recent “flash novel” something out there in the distance pairs shor
 t\, perfectly crystallized prose vignettes with Gail Butensky’s photogra
 phs of the American West. Riding shotgun is Irena Smith\, whose memoir Tro
 ika is a modern-day Odyssey set in California’s Central Coast\, as three
  generations of women share profound family stories and create new ones. A
 s for Angelica Glass\, she’ll opt out of driving altogether—her memoir
  Scavenging Beauty relates her quest to find healing while traversing all 
 the streets in Santa Cruz County by foot. In true travelogue style\, their
  conversation will be accompanied by photos illustrating each author’s j
 ourney. Doors at 6:30pm.\n\nFree\nKALW Public Media\n\nDetails: https://do
 thebay.com/events/2026/10/21/litquake-california-journeys-tickets\nSource:
  DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/litquake-californi
