BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy Lecture: Living with the Stars on the Day of the Dead (S
 F’s Randall Museum)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T203000
DTSTAMP:20261018T205153Z
UID:funcheap-1637875@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:Join the San Francisco Amateur Astronomers for this free event
 . We are thrilled to welcome Dr Isabel Hawkins\, Emeritus Exploratorium. A
 s always\, come a few minutes early for the best snacks!\nEquinoxes and so
 lstices are familiar astronomical markers of the seasons\, but the cross-q
 uarter days—the halfway points between them—are less commonly consider
 ed in popular culture. At the latitude of some of the oldest Maya cities i
 n Mesoamerica\, the cross-quarter day between the September equinox and De
 cember solstice coincides with the season of corn harvest and the traditio
 ns of Day of the Dead. These traditions reflect a rich intersection of Ind
 igenous astronomy\, agricultural cycles\, and the enduring practice of hon
 oring and welcoming the ancestors. Solar events\, including the zenith and
  nadir passages of the Sun\, as well as the November meridional culminatio
 n of the Pleiades\, have important cultural and astronomical connections t
 o this season.\nA Day of the Dead altar or “ofrenda” will invite audie
 nce interaction—we ask interested participants to please bring a persona
 lly meaningful belonging\, or portrait of a dearly departed\, to place on 
 the altar for the duration of the evening and take it home afterward\, cre
 ating a temporary shared space for remembrance and connection.\n\nIsabel H
 awkins\, Ph.D.\, is an astronomer and Emerita at the Exploratorium in San 
 Francisco\, whose work bridges science\, culture\, and public engagement. 
 Born and raised in Córdoba\, Argentina\, she earned her doctorate...\n\nF
 ree\n\nTickets: https://www.sfaa-astronomy.org/public-events/lectures/lect
 ures_2026/oct21_2026\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/astronomy-lecture-l
 iving-stars-day-dead-sfs-randall-museum/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Living
 withStars.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261018T205153Z
LOCATION:Randall Museum\, 199 Museum Way\, San Francisco CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/astronomy-lecture-living-stars-day-dead-sfs-ra
 ndall-museum/
END:VEVENT
