 oin us for the District 1 Richmond Family Summit! The This Is Your City: F
 amily Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and com
 munity members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our c
 ity.\n\nThursday\, Oct. 22\, 2026\, 5:00 p.m. - 7:30 p.m.\n\nRichmond Recr
 eation Center\, 251 18th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94121\n\nFree food\, chi
 ldcare\, and interpretation are provided. Please note all interpretation r
 equests must be made 48 hours or more prior to the Family Summit.\n\nWho s
 hould attend? Everyone is welcome. This event highlights District 1\, but 
 you can attend any Family Summit that fits your schedule.\n\nWhy are we ga
 thering? The Family Summit Series is part of San Francisco's first Citywid
 e Community Needs Assessment. Through conversations with families across t
 he city\, we're learning what matters most to children\, youth\, young adu
 lts\, and families. What we learn will help improve future planning\, prog
 rams\, and services.\n\nWhether you've lived in San Francisco your whole l
 ife or recently made it your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\n\n
 District 1 Neighborhoods include: Inner Richmond\, Central Richmond\, Oute
 r Richmond\, Vista del Mar\, Seacliff\, Lake District\, Presidio Terrace\,
  Lone Mountain\, Golden Gate Park\, Lincoln Park\, and the University of S
 an Fr...\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Department of Children\, Youth & Their Fam
 ilies (DCYF)\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/district-1
