DESCRIPTION:Litquake 2026: SF’s Literature Festival w/ 170+ Events + 600
  Authors (Oct. 8-24)\nNate Paluga\nLitquake\, San Francisco’s Literary F
 estival runs October 8-24\, 2026 with satellite events running from Septem
 ber through January. 170+ events\, 600+ authors and performers\, all over 
 the Bay Area\, and almost ALL for FREE!\nVisit litquake.org or see the ful
 l schedule and tickets.\nAnd it’s capped by the epic “Lit Crawl” on 
 Saturday\, October 24\, 2026 – with 50+ authors and close to 5\,000 fans
  for the world’s largest free pop-up literary event.\nLitquake\, San Fra
 ncisco’s annual literary festival\, was founded by Bay Area writers in o
 rder to put on a week-long literary spectacle for book lovers\, complete w
 ith cutting-edge panels\, unique cross-media events\, and hundreds of read
 ings. Litquake seeks to foster interest in literature\, perpetuate a sense
  of literary community\, and provide a vibrant forum for Bay Area writing 
 as a complement to the city’s music\, film\, and cultural festivals.\n\n
 View this post on Instagram\n\nA post shared by Litquake (@litquake)\n\nUp
 coming Litquake 2026: SF’s Literature Festival w/ 170+ Events + 600 Auth
 ors (Oct. 8-24) Events\nThu 10/22 Litquake 2026: SF’s Literature Festiva
 l w/ 170+ Events + 600 Authors (Oct. 8-24)Disclaimer: Please double check 
 event information with the event organizer as events can be canceled\, det
 ails can change after they are added to our calendar\, and errors do occur
 .\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.litquake.org/\nDetails: https://sf.funch
 eap.com/litquake-2026-sfs-literature-festival-w-170-events-600-authors-oct
 -8-24/\nSource: Funcheap SF
