DESCRIPTION:Get your tickets to the opening and exhibition unveiling of SO
 MArts' "In Their Name: Día de Los Muertos 2026"! The evening features a D
 ía de los Muertos inspired artist market with local vendors and makers\, 
 along with a special performance by Las Hijas de la Madre.\n\nCurated by B
 ridgètt Rex and Rio Yañez\, "In Their Name: Dia de Los Muertos 2026" che
 rishes the ancestral memory\, love\, and devotion carried and embodied by 
 mother figures across generations. In keeping with the tradition of Día d
 e los Muertos\, the exhibition also includes personal altars dedicated to 
 loved ones who have passed.\n\nAbout Las Hijas de la Madre\n\nLas Hijas de
  la Madre are a queer Chicanx feminist punk band featuring Amalia Ortiz (l
 yricist and lead singer)\, Errezeta (lead guitar\, vocals)\, Lilith Tijeri
 na (bass\, vocals)\, Sarah Tijerina (vocals\, keyboard)\, Dr. Kip Austin H
 inton (rhythm guitar and musical direction)\, and Joaquin Muerte (drums).\
 n\nFronted by Amalia Ortiz\, an American Book Award winner for Oral Litera
 ture\, Las Hijas de la Madre center Tejana voices and explore the connecti
 on between Chicanx rasquachismo and the DIY ethos of punk. Through an inte
 rsectional feminist lens\, they radically re-envision a historically white
 \, male expression of punk.\n\nGraphic design by Melanie Cervantes\n\n$15\
 , youth under 16 free\; NOTAFLOF\nSOMArts Cultural Center\n\nDetails: http
 s://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/23/in-their-name-dia-de-los-muertos-2026-t
 ickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/da-
 de-los-muertos-2026/
