DESCRIPTION:@sunset.trading.postSunday\, October 25\, 2026 is the final da
 y of the Sunset Trading Post\, a community-run free-exchange station near 
 48th Avenue and Moraga Street in the Outer Sunset. Visitors can leave a sm
 all craft\, toy\, trinket\, or note and take an item in return. The host s
 tates that the post will close at the end of the day but no specific opera
 ting hours are listed.\nOriginal Event Description:\n_Sunday\, Oct. 25\, 2
 026 is the final day ever of the DIY community-driving Sunset Trading Post
  – There’s no specific hours\, but according to the host on an Instagr
 am post\, it will close “end of day’The Sunset Trading Post (often cal
 led the Outer Sunset Trinket Trade or Sunset Trading Post) is a neighborho
 od free-exchange station in San Francisco’s Outer Sunset District. Locat
 ed near 48th Avenue and Moraga Street\, it operates like a tiny free libra
 ry where visitors leave a small craft\, toy\, or trinket and take one in r
 eturn\n• Location: 48th Avenue and Moraga Street\, Outer Sunset District
 \nCommunity-driven “take a trinket\, leave a trinket” box or shelf\n
 • Common Items: Small art pieces\, handmade crafts\, stickers\, pins\, k
 eychains\, and tiny toys\nleave a note or a small item of equal joy for th
 e next person\nWe love to see arts\, crafts\, pre-loved objects\, and vint
 age items. There is always someone looking for what you’d like to trade.
  There is no need to completely fill this trading post. Trendy items in bu
 lk aren’t necessary to trade here. We see a lot of trinket trade items c
 ontinuing to...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com/p/DewtTzizcQ
 D/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/final-day-sfs-cute-sunset-trading-pos
 t-trinket-exchange-outer-sunset/\nSource: Funcheap SF
