SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:- Class Time: 12:00PM - 3:00PM\n\nIn Beginner's Leatherworking
 : Craft Your Own Tri-fold Leather Journal\, you will learn and apply leath
 erworking techniques to create a custom\, refillable journal from vegetabl
 e tanned leather! We will teach you how to use a pattern to mark and punch
  holes\, set eyelets\, and attach a leather pocket using either saddle sti
 tching or rivets. You will also learn the basics of leather stamping and s
 taining as you customize the journal cover and interior pocket. Finally\, 
 you will install the elastic band\, add your journal inserts\, and finish 
 the piece with a custom button or charm. Finished journals measure approxi
 mately 6" X 8.25" when closed and can hold up to three Large Moleskine Cah
 ier journals (5" X 8.25")\, or standard A5 journals. Each student will lea
 ve class with one handmade leather journal and a working knowledge of the 
 tools and techniques needed to continue exploring leatherworking at home!\
 n\nSupplies Needed: None. All leather supplies are included to complete th
 is project. Each student will also receive two Moleskine journals in eithe
 r ruled or plain page styles to complete their refillable leather journal.
 \n\nThe rules / important stuff: We have a NO EXCEPTIONS 72 HOUR CANCELLAT
 ION policy - this includes cancellation\, re-books\, gift certificates\, m
 oving classes\, etc. For more information on canceling a class\, please re
 ad our cancellation policy. All classes are 21+. If any questions\, please
  email us at info AT workshopsf DOT org.\n\nALL CLASSE...\n\n$73.75\n\nDet
 ails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/25/beginner-s-leatherworking-cra
 ft-your-own-tri-fold-leather-journal-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
