BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PBS Film Preview: Lynn Novick's "Crime and Punishment in America"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T200000
DTSTAMP:20261025T205626Z
UID:dothebay-17811253@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Screening and Conversation\nCo-presented by Commonwealth Club 
 World Affairs & KQED Live\n\nHow did the United States become the world’
 s leading incarcerator? Join acclaimed filmmaker Lynn Novick for a preview
  of her forthcoming PBS documentary\, Crime and Punishment in America\, ex
 ecutive produced by Ken Burns and Sam Pollard.\n\nShe’ll join the film
 ’s consulting producer Rahsaan Thomas\, former co-host of the Peabody Aw
 ard-winning podcast “Ear Hustle” and executive director of Empowerment
  Avenue\, alongside correctional wellness advocate Stephen B. Walker\, and
  survivor advocates Jess and Annie Nichol\, for a compelling conversation 
 on the four-century history of criminal justice in America\, and how Ameri
 cans have wrestled with the problem of crime\, the purpose of punishment a
 nd the meaning of justice. Much like the series\, this conversation will f
 eature differing perspectives from people who have been part of this imper
 fect system that continues to influence nearly all parts of our society.\n
 \nSupport for the film:\nMajor funding was provided by The Atlantic Philan
 thropies\, Emerson Collective\, The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation\, and the 
 Park Foundation.\n\nAdditional support was provided by the National Endowm
 ent for the Humanities\, The Arthur Vining Davis Foundations\, the William
  R. Kenan Jr. Charitable Trust\, Ford Foundation | JustFilms.\n\nAnd by Th
 e Better Angels Society members: John and Catherine Debs\; Timothy Fazio\;
  Lisa Strickler and Mark Gallogly\; the Laurie M. Tisch Illumination Fund.
 ..\n\nTickets: https://www.kqed.org/event/6817/pbs-film-preview-lynn-novic
 ks-crime-and-punishment-in-america\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2
 026/10/27/pbs-film-preview-lynn-novick-s-crime-and-punishment-in-america-t
 ickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/pbs
 -film-preview-lynn-novicks-crime-punishment-america/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34278208/7fed86a3-4c08-4afc-a54c-035453fec3bc.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T205626Z
LOCATION:KQED LIVE\, The Commons\, KQED Headquarters - 2601 Mariposa Stree
 t\, San Francisco\, CA 94110\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/27/pbs-film-preview-lynn-novick-s-
 crime-and-punishment-in-america-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One City One Book: Cities as Ancestors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:dothebay-17914044@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Explore how our relationships with cities\, parks and the more
 -than-human world can shape our future. Inspired by Susanna Kwan's Awake i
 n the Floating City\, the 2026 One City One Book selection\, this conversa
 tion brings together local community leaders working on place-based enviro
 nmental justice to consider what it means to be an ancestor and how the pl
 aces we inhabit become part of our collective legacy.\n\nDrawing on five y
 ears of the Parks as Ancestors series\, inspired by the book\, What Kind o
 f Ancestor Do You Want to Be?\, the discussion expands the conversation be
 yond protected parklands to consider urban spaces as living legacies.\n\nT
 his interactive program invites participants to consider what we inherit f
 rom the places and people who came before us-and what we will leave behind
  for those who come after. Attendees are welcome to bring a photograph or 
 a sentimental object honoring someone they have lost\, if they wish to inc
 orporate it into the program.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by San Francisco Public
  Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public Library\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl
 .org/OCOB-Panel\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/27/one-city-
 one-book-cities-as-ancestors-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\
 n- https://sf.funcheap.com/city-book-cities-ancestors-sf-main-library/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34760574/859caa5b-3764-4937-bce5-ac66dee0ce67.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:Koret Auditorium (SF Public Library)\, 100 Larkin St\, San Franci
 sco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/27/one-city-one-book-cities-as-anc
 estors-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kabbalah of Meaning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T193000
DTSTAMP:20261025T205626Z
UID:funcheap-1640147@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerRabbi DovidJewish Wisdom for a
  Life That Matters\nNo matter how much we achieve\, something within us st
 ill asks: “Is this it? Isn’t there something more?”\n\nThe Kabbalah 
 of Meaning is a new six-session JLI course exploring the Jewish answer to 
 that question. What are we really searching for—and where can it be foun
 d?\nDrawing on Kabbalah and centuries of Jewish wisdom\, we’ll uncover t
 he essential building blocks of a deeply meaningful life. We’ll explore 
 how purpose can be found in our work\, relationships\, challenges\, accomp
 lishments\, and even the ordinary routines that fill our days.\nYou don’
 t have to revamp your life. You don’t need to meditate on a mountaintop.
  You simply need a new lens through which to see the rich world of meaning
  already woven into every part of your life.\nThoughtful\, practical\, and
  surprisingly relevant\, this course offers fresh perspectives and useful 
 tools for living with greater clarity\, connection\, and intention.\nTry 1
 st class free.\nNo previous Jewish learning required. Come as you are—an
 d bring your questions.\n\n$119.00\n\nTickets: https://www.jewishpetaluma.
 com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/jewish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.ht
 m\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/kabbalah-meaning/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Screen
 shot-2026-10-01-010609.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T205626Z
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Petaluma\, 205 Keller St. #101 Petaluma\,
  CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/kabbalah-meaning/
END:VEVENT
