BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spooky Stories Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T203000
DTSTAMP:20261023T050002Z
UID:dothebay-17984562@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Spooky Stories Night — a community reading of gh
 ost stories\, urban legends\, and tales best told after dark\, featuring f
 ive extraordinary Bay Area horror and speculative fiction authors:\n\n→ 
 Cynthia Gómez\n→ Loren Rhoads\n→ Sumiko Saulson\n→ Kristina Ten\n
 → Tamika Thompson\n\nRSVP isn't required\, but we'd love to know you're 
 coming. Bring a friend\, bring your curiosity\, and settle in for an eveni
 ng built for community\, curiosity\, and a little bit of a chill.\n\nCynth
 ia Gómez is the author of the story collection The Nightmare Box and Othe
 r Stories\, and a Tin House and VONA alumn whose short fiction has publish
 ed in Fantasy Magazine\, Strange Horizons\, Pseudopod\, Nightmare Magazine
 \, and numerous anthologies.\n\nLoren Rhoads is the author of In the Wake 
 of the Templars\, a space opera trilogy. She’s co-author (with Brian Tho
 mas) of the As Above\, So Below books\, a dark urban fantasy duet about a 
 succubus and her angel. Her short stories have appeared in Best New Horror
 \, Strange California\, Fright Mare: Women Write Horror\, Sins of the Sire
 ns: 14 Tales of Dark Desire\, and much more. Unsafe Words is the first ful
 l-length collection of her short fiction.\n\nSumiko Saulson is an award-wi
 nning author of Afrosurrealist and multicultural sci-fi and horror whose l
 atest novel Happiness and Other Diseases is available on Mocha Memoirs Pre
 ss. Sumiko is a cartoonist\, science-fiction\, fantasy and horror writer\,
  editor of Black Magic Women\, Scry of Lust and 100 Black Women in Horror 
 Fiction\, autho...\n\nFREE\nTelegraph Hill Arts and Literature presents:\n
 \nTickets: https://telhil.it/spooky\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/
 2026/10/28/spooky-stories-night-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
