DESCRIPTION:Oct 29 to Nov 8 viewable by appointment\, opening reception Oc
 t 29 5-7pm\n\nJoin San Francisco textile artist Margaret Timbrell for the 
 opening reception of Urban Tapestries\, a solo exhibition at Pacific Felt 
 Factory.\n\nThe exhibition brings together textile works depicting the urb
 an wildlife that live alongside us\, mostly in California landscapes. Timb
 rell uses rug tufting\, embroidery\, quilting\, applique\, felting\, and o
 ther handwork to build scenes that reward a closer look. The series consid
 ers how wildlife adapt to changing places and what their presence says abo
 ut belonging and survival in the city.\n\nThe opening reception is Thursda
 y\, October 29\, 2026\, from 5-7 p.m. at Pacific Felt Factory\, 2830 20th 
 Street\, San Francisco. Enter at the 20th Street gate.\n\nUrban Tapestries
  continues through November 8 and is viewable by appointment after the rec
 eption. For more about the artist\, visit www.margarettimbrell.com.\n\nFre
 e\n\nPresented by Margaret Timbrell.\n\nFree\nMargaret Timbrell\n\nTickets
 : http://www.margarettimbrell.com\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/20
 26/10/29/margaret-timbrell-urban-tapestries-opening-reception-tickets\nSou
 rce: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/urban-wildlife
 -textile-free-art-opening-sf/
