BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening Night // Echoes of the Past: Nature as Metaphor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T200000
DTSTAMP:20261025T205626Z
UID:dothebay-17963931@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:The Francophone Museum is pleased to present Echoes of the Pas
 t: Nature as Metaphor\, a new exhibition by award-winning San Francisco ar
 tist Danièle Erville\, with a special opening night reception on October 
 29th.\n\nLandscapes have always been at the heart of Danièle's work\, whe
 ther painted en plein air or imagined from within. Inspired by Jules Super
 vielle's poem "Le petit bois\," the show brings together drawing\, paintin
 g\, and collage that use trees and landscapes as metaphors for memory and 
 feeling. Each piece is a direct expression of Danièle's interiority at th
 e moment of creation\, and together they show how the things that move us 
 as children can speak to us for a lifetime.\n\nDanièle Erville holds a BA
  from Clark University\, studied at the Maryland Institute College of Art\
 , and graduated from the School of the Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston. Her w
 ork is part of the Photograph Study Collection at the Smithsonian American
  Art Museum and has been exhibited in France\, Boston\, Santa Fe\, and thr
 oughout the Bay Area. See her work on Instagram @danieleervilleart.\n\nJoi
 n us for the opening of the exhibition: meet the artist\, enjoy light refr
 eshments\, and be among the first to see the show.\n\nFree entry\, but kin
 dly RSVP. Doors open 6pm\, artist talk at 6:45pm.\n\nThe Francophone Museu
 m presents\n\nTickets: https://www.francophonemuseum.org/events/opening-ni
 ght-danile-erville\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/29/openin
 g-night-echoes-of-the-past-nature-as-metaphor-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\
 nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/opening-night-echoes-nature-me
 taphor/
