DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerArt House SFIn 2015\, Japan’
 s Empress Michiko chose a gold-leaf cherry-blossom woodblock print by Yows
 aku Sekino for the Imperial Palace. Now 20 of Sekino’s prints are on vie
 w at Art House SF in the Castro\, in what are his only solo exhibitions ou
 tside Japan.\nGallery founder Max Khusid leads a small-group talk standing
  at the prints:\n\nUkiyo-e\, shin-hanga and sōsaku-hanga: three ways Japa
 n made woodblock prints\nHow Japanese prints reached Van Gogh and\, later\
 , Steve Jobs\nHow Sekino layers 10+ hand-carved blocks and applies gold le
 af by hand\nHanakotoba\, the Japanese language of flowers: what each bloom
  on the wall is saying\n\nLimited to 15 people. Tickets are $10\, credited
  toward any purchase. The exhibition itself is free and open Wednesday to 
 Sunday through November 1.\n\n$10.00\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.co
 m/e/gallery-talk-japanese-woodblock-prints-the-language-of-flowers-tickets
 -2003436893680?aff=funcheap\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/japanese-woo
