DESCRIPTION:This virtual introductory workshop provides artists and arts w
 orkers with a foundational understanding of the grant writing process.\nFa
 cilitated by artist and arts administrator Eric Garcia\, the workshop offe
 rs step-by-step guidance for finding and navigating funding opportunities\
 , understanding application requirements\, developing strong grant materia
 ls\, and building confidence in seeking support for creative projects.\nDe
 signed for people who are new to grant writing or looking to strengthen th
 eir foundational skills\, the workshop emphasizes practical tools and appr
 oaches that participants can apply to future funding opportunities. The wo
 rkshop has a particular emphasis on live performance\, though artists and 
 arts workers from all disciplines are welcome.\nThis workshop takes place 
 virtually via Zoom. The meeting link will be provided upon registration. L
 ive auto-captioning will be available.\nDetour Productions offers sliding-
 scale tuition and No One Turned Away for Lack of Funds. Participants seeki
 ng a NOTAFLOF registration code or wishing to share access needs may conta
 ct directors@detour.productions.\n\n$50-$200.\n\nPresented by Detour Produ
 ctions\n\n$50-$200.\nDetour Productions\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.i
