DESCRIPTION:Free Outdoor Video Art Walk Through SF’s Mid-Market (Oct. 30
  – Nov. 1)\nN/A\nMeet the Moment Video Festival brings politically and s
 ocially engaged video art to storefront windows\, vacant spaces and outdoo
 r projections along a walkable Mid-Market loop. Curated by Natasha Becker\
 , Mushi Wooseong James\, Việt Lê\, Julio César Morales\, Efe Ozmen and
  Twyla Ruby\, the festival features artists including Dread Scott\, Suzann
 e Lacy\, Claudia Rankine & John Lucas\, and Bruce Yonemoto & Karen Finley.
  Presented by Meet the Moment\, a Bay Area coalition initiated by TnT Art 
 Lab.\nMid-Market walking loop: from Root Division (1131 Mission St) along 
 Market St\, through Yerba Buena Lane to YBCA\, and back along Mission St\n
 \nUpcoming Free Outdoor Video Art Walk Through SF’s Mid-Market (Oct. 30 
 – Nov. 1) Events\nFri 10/30 Free Outdoor Video Art Walk Through SF’s M
 id-Market (Oct. 30 – Nov. 1)Disclaimer: Please double check event inform
 ation with the event organizer as events can be canceled\, details can cha
 nge after they are added to our calendar\, and errors do occur.\n\nFree\n\
 nTickets: https://www.meetthemoment.us/video-festival.html\nDetails: https
 ://sf.funcheap.com/free-outdoor-video-art-walk-midmarket-sf/\nSource: Func
