BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Taxidermy Rat Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17672037@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Calling someone a "rat" is generally seen as a bad thing—but
  is it really? As the owner of several rats (yes\, the guy writing this co
 py)\, I can tell you firsthand that rats are amazing\, cute\, and very cle
 an animals. Sure\, they get hit with the whole “Well\, the Black Plague 
 was their fault” thing\, but we all know it was really the fleas. No exp
 erience? No problem. This class is perfect for anyone looking to dip their
  toes into the world of taxidermy. We’ll walk (scurry?) you through ever
 y step. You’ll leave with a newfound skill\, a tiny new friend\, and pro
 bably a weird story to tell at parties.\n\nThe instructor\, Mr. Vassallo h
 as over thirty-five years experience as a professional taxidermist and tea
 cher. He has traveled Continental North America\, Alaska\, Hawaii\, Mexico
 \, Europe and Africa studying\, collecting and preserving wildlife.\n\nImp
 ortant Details:\nClasses will be held at 766 Valencia St.\, San Francisco\
 nPre-registration required as materials must be prepared for each student 
 and space is VERY limited.\nChildren under 18 must be accompanied by an ad
 ult. We ask that all attendees be over the age of 14. Special exceptions m
 ay be made by contacting us before you purchase your spot.\nStudents are e
 ncouraged to bring lunch/snacks.\nPlease arrive promptly at the start time
 .\nCancellations must be made at least 72 hours prior to the date of the c
 lass. Cancellations will then be converted to credit that can either be us
 ed toward merchandise in the store or to enroll in another workshop....\n\
 n$225\, 18+ or with Guardian\nPaxton Gate's\n\nTickets: https://paxtongate
 .com/products/taxidermy-rat-class\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/20
 26/10/31/diy-taxidermy-rat-workshop-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
