SUMMARY:Plant Wisdom for Day of the Dead: Acacia Confusa + Syrian Rue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
DTSTAMP:20261011T195433Z
UID:dothebay-17947100@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Some plants come with thousands of years of stories attached. 
 In this two-hour workshop\, Jennifer Langford explores Acacia confusa and 
 Syrian rue\, two plants with long histories of ceremonial and ancestral us
 e. You'll learn where they come from\, how different cultures have underst
 ood and worked with them\, and the traditions that have gathered around th
 em over time. Held on Day of the Dead\, it's a fitting moment to think abo
 ut memory\, lineage\, and how plant knowledge gets handed from one generat
 ion to the next. The afternoon closes with a non-psychedelic tea offering 
 and a guided Yoga Nidra practice\, so you'll leave both smarter and deeply
  relaxed. To skip the ticket fees\, register in person at the Church of Mo
 ther Gong.\n\n$40\n\nTickets: https://www.mothergong.com/events-2-1/acacia
 -confusa-syrian-rue-workshop\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11
 /1/plant-wisdom-for-day-of-the-dead-acacia-confusa-syrian-rue-tickets\nSou
 rce: DoTheBay
