 \n--Open to people of all genders.Workshop Description:\nBondage Fundament
 als is an four-session introductory course designed for those new to rope 
 bondage\, providing foundational skills\, terminology\, and safety practic
 es. The course focuses on floor-based rope work\, influenced primarily by 
 Japanese bondage (shibari/kinbaku)\, while integrating techniques from var
 ious traditions. Participants will learn essential ties\, structural eleme
 nts\, and the principles of Risk-Aware Consensual Kink (RACK) to foster sa
 fer practice. Emphasis on communication\, consent\, pleasure\, and injury 
 prevention\, including awareness of possible bodily and emotional trauma. 
 By the end of the course\, students will have the confidence to continue t
 heir bondage education independently or in advanced non-suspension classes
 . For in-depth information about workshop learning objectives and the cour
 se in general\, check out the course syllabus.\nSkill level and Prerequisi
 tes:\nThis course is meant to introduce you to rope bondage. It assumes th
 at you have never touched a rope before and don’t know any bondage termi
 nology. A familiarity with a single column tie is extremely helpful\, but 
 not at all necessary. By the end of the course\, you will h...\n\n$360\nBi
