CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:For one night\, the Alliance Française de San Francisco & the
  Francophone Museum of San Francisco will transform into a 1920s speakeasy
 .\n\nStep back into les années folles and into an evening of live music\,
  dancing\, and Jazz Age glamour.When Prohibition threatened to dry out Cal
 ifornia\, French winemakers and traditions helped keep the state's wine al
 ive\, one more thread tying France and California together. Tonight we exp
 lore that history\, with Prohibition-era cocktails and wines to sip and a 
 Francophone buffet to savor.\n\nTickets: $60 general\, $50 for AFSF member
 s\, in advance only. $80 at the door. TICKETS HERE.\n\nTicket holders will
  receive a secret password and instructions for entry.\n\nGrab your ticket
 \, don your flapper best\, and we'll see you on the other side of the door
 .\n\nAbout our speaker\, Rebecca Yerger\nRebecca A. Yerger is an historian
  whose focus is to honor and preserve the cultural heritage of her lifelon
 g home – the Napa Valley. As part of this endeavor she has authored Memo
 ry Lane\, a history column published by the Napa Valley Register newspaper
 \, for over 31 years. Her credentials also include Napa Valley centric vid
 eo productions filmed by PBS\, NHK\, NATIVA and the Travel Channel as well
  as written articles for various print publications.\n\nMeet our live band
 s for the night\nCharles Unger Experience\nA major force in the music scen
 e of the San Francisco Bay area for the last 40 years\, saxophonist Charle
 s Unger is a musical institution. He is known for his exuberant sty...\n\n
 $50 for members\; $60 public entry. 21+\nThe Alliance Française and Franc
 ophone Museum present\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3
 A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe%2Fla-nuit-au-musee-a-sip-of-the-roaring-20s-
 nov-5-2026-tickets-2001940316377\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/202
 6/11/5/la-nuit-au-musee-a-sip-of-the-roaring-20s-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
