DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 8pm / Show 8:30pm\n\n$17 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nEternities (Katie Porter & Bob Bellerue) unfold their 
 collaboration of sustained tones on bass clarinet\, with zither\, harmonic
 a\, whistling\, and electronic feedback. Inspired by deep presence\, reson
 ant feedback\, melodic drone\, and overtone magic\, their work is an intui
 tive exploration of sound. Bellerue will also perform a solo set utilizing
  electronics and resonant feedback through The Lab’s grand piano. Photo 
 of Eternities by Peter Gannushkin.\n\nAntimatter\, the solo performance pr
 oject of Xopher Davidson\, grew out of a childhood building radios and sou
 ndmakers\, and developed into a practice built from industrial oscillators
  and military surplus equipment. An associate of Zbigniew Karkowski\, Mary
 anne Amacher\, and many others\, Davidson has released records on Asphodel
 \, Daydream Library Series\, Sub Rosa (with Karkowski)\, and others.\n\n$1
 7\n\nTickets: https://link.dice.fm/td9b75b1d00f\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/11/6/eternities-bob-bellerue-katie-porter-antimatter-tick
 ets\nSource: DoTheBay
