BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ZooLights at San Francisco Zoo (Nov. 6-Jan 3)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T191250Z
UID:funcheap-1640538@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Kids Families
DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Zoo & GardensSan Francisco Zoo & Gardens is thri
 lled to announce its all-new\, two-month-long ZooLights evening holiday pr
 ogram that will light up the Zoo in spectacular fashion from November 6 th
 rough January 3\, 2027. The nighttime event represents the return of ZooLi
 ghts\, which the Zoo last hosted in 2018.\n\n“The Zoo is the perfect ven
 ue for a safe\, outdoor holiday lights experience\,” said Cassandra Cost
 ello\, CEO and Executive Director. “We have taken this event to the next
  level\, creating 14 dazzling zones\, with winter\, botanical or animal-th
 emed components. It’s going to be truly breathtaking\, and a great exper
 ience for the entire family.”\n\nIn addition to traditional holiday zone
 s\, where guests will walk through awe-inspiring lighted tunnels and strol
 l among giant candy canes\, giant ornaments and gift boxes\, there’s an 
 entire frozen zone\, with 10-foot-tall icicles\, sparkling snowflakes\, a 
 frozen forest\, a massive ice throne and frozen sleigh for that perfect fa
 mily photo.\n\n“The effect will be magical\,” said Costello. “Overal
 l\, ZooLights will have more than one million lights\, and the walk-throug
 h areas include amazing photo ops\, and nods to the City of San Francisco 
 with a Golden Gate Bridge and the iconic cable car.”\n\nWhimsical animal
  shapes and scenes will dot the landscape\, using 2D and 3D illuminations 
 of a rhino and gorilla\, even a tree full of ring-tailed lemurs. Vibrantly
  colored\, larger-than-life butterflies are part of an enchanting botanica
 l pathway\,...\n\n$30.00\n\nTickets: https://www.sfzoo.org\nDetails: https
 ://sf.funcheap.com/zoolights-san-francisco-zoo-nov-6jan-3/\nSource: Funche
 ap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Butter
 fly-photo-op.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T191250Z
LOCATION:San Francisco Zoo & Gardens\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/zoolights-san-francisco-zoo-nov-6jan-3/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Destination: Cosmos–An Experiential Sound Voyage by Christopher 
 Willits + Envelop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTSTAMP:20261017T204148Z
UID:dothebay-17811263@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Destination: Cosmos\nAn Experiential Sound Voyage by Christoph
 er Willits and Envelop\n\nFriday\, November 6 | The Loom\, Oakland\n\nEigh
 ty years ago\, for the very first time\, humanity laid eyes on the first p
 icture of Earth taken from space. In celebration of the 80th anniversary\,
  KQED\, sound artist Christopher Willits\, Envelop and Chabot Space & Scie
 nce Center are launching you into the deep cosmos. Step inside a 360-degre
 e sphere of mesmerizing light and 3D immersive sound. The listening experi
 ence is a mix of Christopher Willits’ live ambient performance and his a
 cclaimed score SPACE\, woven with rocket launches and the distinct electro
 magnetic hum of stars\, planets\, and the galaxy.\n\nDon’t miss this unf
 orgettable\, multi-sensory moment to get together in honor of our blue pla
 net and beyond.\n\n$45-$55\, All ages\nKQED Live Presents\n\nTickets: http
 ://tixr.com/pr/DTBCosmos/204379\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026
 /11/6/destination-cosmos-an-experiential-sound-voyage-by-christopher-willi
 ts-and-envelop-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34278252/ede327a6-65fb-409d-9f4d-ace2bc45e039.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T204148Z
