BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wendy Clarke: The Prison Tapes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T063000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T083000
DTSTAMP:20261019T210249Z
UID:dothebay-17969871@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Wendy Clarke\, Inside Out (still)\, 2002\n\nDoors 6pm / Screen
 ing 6:30pm\n\nFree\n\nA screening and conversation with Wendy Clarke and N
 igel Poor\, presented in collaboration with Cushion Works and Ear Hustle o
 n the occasion of the exhibition Wendy Clarke: The Prison Tapes on view th
 rough Nov. 14\, 2026.\n\nWendy Clarke is a video pioneer whose practice sp
 ans more than five decades. The daughter of avant-garde filmmaker Shirley 
 Clarke\, she has spent her career positioning the camera as a tool for int
 imacy\, dialogue\, and human connection across social and institutional bo
 undaries. She is best known for Love Tapes\, a collection of over 2\,500 v
 ideo recordings of people talking about love.\n\nIn conjunction with The P
 rison Tapes (1979-2002)\, an exhibition on view at Cushion Works through N
 ovember 14\, The Lab presents an evening with Clarke. The program includes
  a screening of rarely-seen video work and a discussion with the artist Ni
 gel Poor\, co-founder and co-host of Ear Hustle\, the first podcast create
 d and produced inside a prison. Their conversation will be recorded and pr
 esented as a special episode of the podcast.\n\nFor several years in the 1
 980s and 90s\, Clarke was an artist in residence within the California pri
 son system—at the Ventura Youth Correctional Facility\, the California I
 nstitution for Men in Chino\, and the CIM Del Norte facility\, working pri
 marily with men in the HIV/AIDS unit. In dingy dayrooms and with minimal r
 esources\, she created the conditions for exchange and discovery...\n\nDet
 ails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/wendy-clarke-the-prison-tapes-
 tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35021409/414b03aa-2bd8-4fd7-be83-b7b1c5b25980.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019T210249Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/wendy-clarke-the-prison-tapes-ti
 ckets
END:VEVENT
