DESCRIPTION:A runaway hit with families at last year’s festival\, Leap! 
 is back by popular demand!\n\nBring the whole family for a free screening 
 of the animated feature film "Leap!" (rated PG)\, a heartwarming adventure
  about courage\, friendship\, and following your dreams. Set in 19th-centu
 ry Paris\, the story follows Félicie\, a spirited orphan determined to be
 come a ballerina\, and her best friend Victor\, an aspiring inventor. Toge
 ther they escape their orphanage and chase their passions in the City of L
 ights\, where Félicie must summon all her determination to pursue the rol
 e of a lifetime at the Paris Opera Ballet.\n\nPerfect for aspiring young a
 rtists\, this event will include an introduction by San Francisco Ballet P
 rincipal Dancer Dores André and a short opportunity for participants to d
 ance onstage after the screening.\n\nAdmission is free\, with a suggested 
 donation of $10/child and $15/adult. Registration is required: https://eve
 nts.humanitix.com/leap-sfdff2026/tickets\n\nFree\n2026 SF Dance Film Festi
 val:\n\nTickets: https://sfdancefilmfest.org/fall-festival-2026/leap/\nDet
 ails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8/leap-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
 \n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/2026-dance-film-fest-free-l
 eap-screening-onstage-dance-sf/
