CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Prize-winning historian Kevin Waite uncovers an extraordinary 
 story of survival in this first book-length biography of Biddy Mason. The 
 narrative follows Mason's journey from the cotton South to metropolitan Ca
 lifornia\, detailing how she crossed the continent\, broke free from slave
 ry\, and built Black Los Angeles.\n\nThrough the lens of the Civil War\, R
 econstruction\, and the dawn of Jim Crow\, Waite reveals Mason's profound 
 impact on California's history.\n****\nABOUT THIS EVENT\nThis event will b
 e hosted by Book Passage at our Corte Madera store.\nFree Admission / Open
  Seating\nFollowing the presentation\, there will be a signing line or a m
 eet-and-greet.\nIf you are unable to attend the event\, you can still get 
 your copy by clicking the "BUY THE BOOK" button above. If you would like a
  signed or personalized book\, please note that in the order comment field
 .\nFor any questions regarding our events\, please contact us at books@boo
 kpassage.com.\n\nFree\nBook Passage Presents:\n\nTickets: https://bookpass
 age.com/event/kevin-waite-boundless-biddy-mason\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/11/8/kevin-waite-the-boundless-biddy-mason-tickets\nSourc
 e: DoTheBay
