SUMMARY:What Makes a Day Enough? A Self-Love Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T210000
DTSTAMP:20261014T214646Z
UID:dothebay-17955534@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Experiences
DESCRIPTION:You did so much today. Why does it still feel like it wasn’t
  enough?\nWhat Makes a Day Enough? is a 90-minute self-love circle for any
 one feeling overwhelmed\, behind\, or caught in the pressure to keep doing
  more.\nThrough guided reflection\, journaling\, and supportive conversati
 on\, we’ll explore:\n• What matters most to us and how we want to show
  up.\n• Where our time and energy are going.\n• The “shoulds” and 
 negative messages that keep us feeling like we haven’t done enough.\n\nT
 ogether\, we’ll make space to question the expectations we carry and con
 sider what makes a day feel meaningful on our own terms.\n\nCome on your o
 wn or bring a friend. No experience is needed\, and sharing is always opti
 onal. Please bring a journal and pen.\n\nHosted by Aileen Morales\, certif
 ied Heal Your Life® Coach and founder of With Joy\, Aileen.\n\nTuesday\, 
 November 10\, 2026\n7:00–8:30 PM\nTantara SF\n914 Pacific Ave\, San Fran
 cisco\n$25 per person\n\nDetails and registration: withjoyaileen.com/enoug
 h\n\n25\nWith Joy\, Aileen presents:\n\nTickets: https://withjoyaileen.com
 /enough\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/10/what-makes-a-day-
 enough-a-self-love-circle-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
