DESCRIPTION:Co-presented by The American Craft Council\nCelebrate the prof
 ound connections between people and the objects that shape their lives at 
 Object Stories: San Francisco. Hear from a diverse group of Bay Area artis
 ts\, makers\, and community voices as they each share a handmade object th
 at holds personal significance and tell the story behind it\, revealing ho
 w craft intersects with memory\, identity\, creativity\, and belonging.\n\
 nObject Stories is a signature storytelling series presented by the Americ
 an Craft Council\, a national nonprofit organization dedicated to building
  a world where objects matter\, makers thrive\, and craft connects. Each e
 vent brings together artists\, writers\, and cultural leaders to explore t
 he meaning and impact of craft through personal stories inspired by object
 s they cherish.\n\n$30\n\nTickets: https://craftcouncil.ticketbud.com/obje
