DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerEco SF School Farm Volunteer W
 ork Day | SF\nNational Park Service\nCome join a volunteer work party at T
 he School Farm every second Saturday from noon to 4 pm to lend a hand and 
 learn about farm work.\nAll skill levels and abilities are welcome\, even 
 for moral support and comic relief. They will provide some water and maybe
  a snack\, and plenty of well worn gloves\, but If you’d like\, bring so
 me more refreshments to share or your favorite personal protective equipme
 nt. For more info\, contact sam@eco-sf.org.\n\nThe School Farm is located 
 on the campus of the Academy of Arts and Sciences and the School of the Ar
 ts – 555 Portola Dr. San Francisco. Enter gate on O’shaughnessy Blvd j
 ust before it crosses Portola. It’s close to 36\, 44\, 48\, and 52 Muni 
 lines. From the parking area at the top\, proceed on foot to the right\, d
 own the hill towards the athletic field. Limited parking is available furt
 her down the driveway at the loading dock\, but please do not park on the 
 grass. The farm is behind the east bleachers across the field.\n– Update
 d 6/4/19 – Event info last checked via website\n\nUpcoming Eco SF School
  Farm Volunteer Work Day | SF Events\nSat 10/10 Eco SF School Farm Volunte
 er Work Day | SFSat 11/14 Eco SF School Farm Volunteer Work Day | SFSat 12
 /12 Eco SF School Farm Volunteer Work Day | SFDisclaimer: Please double ch
 eck event information with the event organizer as events can be canceled\,
  details can change after they are added to our calendar\, and err...\n\nF
 ree\n\nTickets: http://www.eco-sf.org\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/ec
 o-sf-school-farm-volunteer-work-day-sf-164/\nSource: Funcheap SF
