BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Abiogenesis” Opening Reception - new works by Philip Beesley 
 & Casey Curran
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T200000
DTSTAMP:20261020T194441Z
UID:dothebay-17955596@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Arts & Family
DESCRIPTION:Heron Arts is pleased to announce Abiogenesis\, a duo exhibiti
 on featuring Philip Beesley and Casey Curran. The opening reception for Ab
 iogenesis is Saturday\, November 14th\, 2026 from 6-9pm. It is free and op
 en to the public and will be part of San Francisco Art Week. The exhibitio
 n will be on view to the public until January 24th\, by appointment only.\
 n\nAbiogenesis brings together the work of Philip Beesley and Casey Curran
  around an elusive phenomenon: the emergence of life from inert matter. Th
 eir work assembles unmistakably artificial elements that\, in their cellul
 ar forms and gentle movement\, begin to suggest life. Lacework becomes mem
 brane. Scaffolds of repeating cells become skeletons of organisms. Glowing
 \, shimmering light evokes the pulses of nature. Mechanical gestures appea
 r to breathe\, bloom\, and reach into the world.\nIntimations of life with
 in Beesley’s and Curran’s sculptures suggest that living form can emer
 ge from the matter of the earth. Beesley and Curran probe this threshold t
 hrough myth\, science\, and sensitive sculptural expression.\n\nArtist Bio
 s\n\nPhilip Beesley is a Canadian artist whose sculptures explore the thre
 shold between inert matter and living form. At the heart of his work are g
 lowing\, pulsing\, precious structures composed of innumerable finely craf
 ted elements. Classically trained in fine art and architecture\, he create
 s immersive installations of lace-like scaffolds and suspended membranes\,
  inviting intimate encounters with light\, texture\, and gen...\n\nFree\nH
 eron Arts presents\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2
 F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe%2Fabiogenesis-new-works-by-philip-beesley-and-c
 asey-curran-tickets-2003420173670%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator%26keep_tld%3Dtrue\
 nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/abiogenesis-opening-recep
 tion-new-works-by-philip-beesley-casey-curran-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\
 nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/free-2026-art-week-opening-kin
 etic-sculpture-show-abiogenesis-sfs-heron-arts/
GEO:37.7746027;-122.4083386
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34956219/0d26a069-aed2-4823-8e25-3276eecb8d66.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T194441Z
LOCATION:Heron Arts\, 7 Heron Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
