BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Minnette Lehmann Memorial Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTSTAMP:20261016T211839Z
UID:dothebay-17961869@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Doors 12pm / Program 1pm / Open Mic 2pm\n\nRSVP Here (& regist
 er for streaming link)\n\nThe Bay Area art community mourns the loss of Mi
 nnette Lehmann\, feminist artist\, intellectual\, educator\, mother\, gran
 dmother\, wife\, and friend to many\, who passed away in June\, just shy o
 f her 98th birthday. Minnette was one of the longest-serving board members
  of The Lab\, serving for nearly 20 years.\n\nPlease gather with us for a 
 memorial and celebration of Minnette’s extraordinary life\, art\, sharp 
 wit\, dry humor\, and indelible legacy. The program will be Emcee’d by K
 athy Brew with music by Richard Marriott. Everyone is welcome. (RSVP for a
  remote online streaming option.)\n\nAbout Minnette\n\nSince the 1940s\, L
 ehmann was at the forefront of important Bay Area intellectual and artisti
 c movements. She hosted countless artists\, thinkers\, and art-world gathe
 rings at her San Francisco home and enchanting garden overlooking the Bay.
 \n\nAn embodiment of the “wild woman” archetype\, she challenged and r
 edefined domestic and artistic institutions for women\, expanding possibil
 ities through photography\, performance art\, collage\, and painting. Her 
 groundbreaking photographic series Trouble in Paradise documented a pivota
 l moment in American history when marriage itself became problematic. She 
 received a National Endowment for the Arts grant for the work.\n\nOver a 2
 0-year teaching career at San Francisco State\, the San Francisco Art Inst
 itute\, and UC Extension\, she mentored generations of artists while conti
 nuall...\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ev
 entbrite.com%2Fe%2Fminnette-lehmann-memorial-celebration-tickets-200302167
 8761%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1
 5/minnette-lehmann-memorial-celebration-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34986877/f6f479d4-3eaf-40a1-874f-dc0fcdc08d3a.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T211839Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/15/minnette-lehmann-memorial-celeb
 ration-tickets
END:VEVENT
