DESCRIPTION:Artist Talk & Pop-Up: “What the Earth Remembers”\n\nCallin
 g all pottery lovers\, ceramics enthusiasts\, and the simply curious! Join
  RedBrick Ceramic Studio on Sunday\, November 22 for an afternoon of art a
 nd community featuring ceramic artist Tasha Colby.\n\nAs a self-taught cer
 amicist\, Tasha’s practice is shaped by curiosity\, experimentation\, ne
 cessity\, and community. In her talk\, she’ll reflect on what it means t
 o take part in a practice that’s been around for thousands of years\, an
 d how working with clay connects us to the past\, the earth\, and each oth
 er.\n\nStick around for a ceramic demonstration and a closer look at Tasha
 ’s creative process and approach to working with clay. Whether you’re 
 an experienced potter\, just getting into ceramics\, or simply curious abo
 ut the craft\, there’s something here for you!\n\nFree and open to every
 one\nLight refreshments provided\n\nCome meet the artist\, connect with fe
 llow pottery lovers\, and spend a Sunday afternoon getting inspired by the
  world of clay. We’d love to see you there!\n\nRedBrick Ceramic Studio:\
 nhttps://www.instagram.com/redbrickceramics\nhttps://redbrickceramic.com/\
 n\nTasha Colby:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/tasha_colby/\n\nFree and open t
 o everyone\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.
 eventbrite.com%2Fe%2F2002985500551%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https:/
 /dothebay.com/events/2026/11/22/redbrick-ceramic-studio-artist-talk-pop-up
 -tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/r
