BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:$1.50 Admission Day for Ripley’s Believe It or Not!’s Final Da
 y in SF
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T180000
DTSTAMP:20261016T211839Z
UID:funcheap-1642840@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Google MapsRipley’s Believe It or Not! is closing its San Fr
 ancisco Odditorium at Fisherman’s Wharf on Dec. 1\, 2026\, ending nearly
  60 years of strange sights at 175 Jefferson St. The attraction first open
 ed on Feb. 2\, 1967\, and it’s sending things off with a suitably weird 
 farewell.\nOn its final day\, admission will cost just $1.50 for adults an
 d 75 cents for kids\, matching the original 1967 ticket prices. Want to vi
 sit before then? Ripley’s is also offering $19.67 admission on Thursdays
  during its final weeks.\nThe museum is auctioning off select exhibits and
  artifacts through a silent auction that stays open until closing. Among t
 he oddities up for grabs are a Golden Gate Bridge made on the head of a pi
 n\, toothpick replicas of the bridge\, Joe DiMaggio’s crutches\, a chick
 en-wire portrait of Janis Joplin\, a matchstick cable car and even a fur-c
 overed fish. There’s also a 1989 Emmy tied to coverage of the Loma Priet
 a earthquake and World Series.\n\nThe building is already being marketed f
 or lease\, so the future of this longtime Wharf attraction remains up in t
 he air.\nH/t SF Chronicle\n\n$1.50\n\nTickets: https://www.ripleys.com/att
 ractions/ripleys-believe-it-or-not-san-francisco\nDetails: https://sf.func
 heap.com/150-admission-day-ripleys-nots-final-day-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Ripley
 s.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T211839Z
LOCATION:Ripley’s Believe It or Not Odditorium\, 175 Jefferson Street\, 
 San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/150-admission-day-ripleys-nots-final-day-sf/
END:VEVENT
