SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Community,Holiday,Kids and Families
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a festive evening at Civic Center Plaza as we illu
 minate the holiday season! The annual Civic Center Plaza Tree Lighting eve
 nt returns December 2\, 4-7pm! Add this fun\, free\, family-friendly event
  to your holiday calendar\; featuring festive performances\, with the nigh
 t’s lineup including music\, performances\, and appearances from The Tap
  Dancing Christmas Trees\, Christmas VIPs and the man-of-the-hour: Santa!\
 nThe event also features “snow” flurries\, where kids (and kids at hea
 rt) can twirl and dance through the falling snow\, and a toy giveaway for 
 the first 500 children 12-and-under\, led by Another Planet Entertainment 
 and the San Francisco Police Department\, with the Civic Center Community 
 Benefit District.\nIn the Makers Village\, SF Etsy will lead holiday-theme
 d activities and the San Francisco Public Library will host a book giveawa
 y. Bites will be available for purchase\, along with a full bar featuring 
 seasonal favorites.\nThe event takes place across from an illuminated City
  Hall in Civic Center Plaza. Event begins promptly at 4pm\, with the light
 ing of Civic Center’s 50-foot noble fir at 5:30pm. Happening rain or shi
 ne!\nSee some footage from years prior here!\nRSVP for an event day remind
 er on Eventbrite.\n\nDetails: https://sfciviccenter.org/event/civic-center
 -plaza-tree-lighting-2026/\nSource: SF Civic Center
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T212911Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sfciviccenter.org/event/civic-center-plaza-tree-lighting-2026/
END:VEVENT
