DESCRIPTION:“Legion of Honor” Museum Free Day (First Tuesdays)\n© Ste
 phanHoerold Getty Images Signature via Canva.com\nThe Legion of Honor disp
 lays a collection of 4\,000 years of ancient and European art in an exquis
 ite Beaux-Arts building in an unforgettable setting overlooking the Golden
  Gate Bridge.\nNormally\, general admission is $20 for adults\, but on the
  first Tuesday of the month\, admission is free.\n\nThis offer applies onl
 y to the permanent collection galleries. Full-price admission to special e
 xhibitions still applies.\nWe suggest booking your tickets in advance onli
 ne.\nFree admission may also be redeemed by visiting the ticketing and mem
 bership desks\, pending availability.\n\nOther Free & Discounted Admission
  Deals\nThe Legion of Honor offers several programs for free or reduced ad
 mission to permanent galleries and special exhibitions. Details on these p
 rograms are outlined below.\nWe will require timed tickets for every visit
 or\, including general admission. To ensure your preferred time slot\, ple
 ase reserve your entry date and time in advance online.\n\nFree Saturdays 
 for Bay Area Residents\nReserve Online and Skip the Line\nEvery Saturday\,
  the Legion of Honor offers free general admission to all residents of the
  nine Bay Area counties. Saturdays feature engaging art experiences for th
 e entire family\, including art making\, gallery guides\, and tours with d
 iscussion and sketching in the permanent galleries.\n\nThis offer applies 
 only to the permanent collection galleries. Full-price admission...\n\nFre
 e\n\nTickets: https://legionofhonor.famsf.org/free-reduced-admission\nDeta
 ils: https://sf.funcheap.com/legion-of-honor-museum-free-day-first-tuesday
